                                "sense_id": "3d00335a-7e2e-326e-b24f-eb7f26872df5",
                                "text": "Mark Stoyle, however, has argued that the 'glotticide' of the Cornish language was mainly a result of the Cornish gentry adopting English to dissociate themselves from the reputation for disloyalty and rebellion associated with the Cornish language since the 1497 uprising.",
